{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAowGqVDeFNy4rsL1beF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The job was running every night and failing, and the script then crashed before it could send you the failure note. I haven't run any of this, since it needs your real home directory, keychain and Telegram. I only checked that the script parses and the plist is valid.\n\n**Causes**\n- **Job did run:** `launchctl-print.txt` shows `runs = 6` and `last exit code = 1`. The job fired every night at 02:30.\n- **Not logged in:** `claude` printed \"Not logged in\" every night. The plist sets no `USER`, so the CLI can't find your login in the keychain.\n- **Read-only variable:** `status=$?` at line 19 of `nightly-review.zsh` kills the script, because `status` is read-only in zsh. That happened before the `notify.sh` failure call, so no failure note was ever sent.\n\n**Fixes**\n- **Script:** I changed `status=$?` to `rc=$?`, added `< /dev/null` to the `claude` call, and log the exit code and duration to stderr. An empty output file now counts as a failure, and a failing `notify.sh` is logged and makes the script exit non-zero.\n- **Plist:** I added `USER=vk` under `EnvironmentVariables`.\n\n**Your colleague's note**\n- **Applied:** use `launchctl print` first, avoid `status`, set `USER`, close stdin, log duration, and don't trust the exit code alone.\n- **Didn't apply:** piping the prompt over stdin. Your prompt arrives fine, and the failure was the login, not missing input. Their 16:50 schedule and \"no evidence it ran\" also don't match your case.\n\n`ANSWER.md` has the full write-up. To apply the fix, copy the files back to your home directory and reload the job with `launchctl bootout` then `bootstrap`. After that, run `launchctl kickstart -k gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review`. Check that the exit code is 0, the output file is fresh, the run took a plausible time, and the Telegram message arrives. Then force a failure once to confirm the failure note arrives too. If \"Not logged in\" persists, the keychain may not be reachable from a background job. In that case, run `/login` in `claude` from a normal terminal session."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1994,"cache_read_input_tokens":24256,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1994},"output_tokens":723,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"08ce31c7-3497-4f9a-8f63-bf56eedbd9e3","uuid":"cce2d7f5-aa3f-4d26-a6e0-47a6518afb0d","timestamp":"2026-10-19T02:30:50.293Z","request_id":"req_011CgAowGbbVprXNQgvGQXFR"}
